The real subtlety: when there are 5 titles with remaining copies, forming a group of 5 is not always optimal. For example, when the counts are [3,3,3,3,2] (the "two each of the first 4 books, one each of the rest" case: counts = [2,2,2,2,1], total 9 books, expected 5560).

